  "decision": "**Rating**: Overweight\n\n**Executive Summary**: Initiate a scaled entry into NVDA, allocating 2.5% of the portfolio to capture the current pullback while maintaining the ability to add if the stock tests lower support. Implement a disciplined, wide-stop approach that accounts for the current 6.06 ATR to avoid being shaken out by near-term technical volatility. Target accumulation near the 200-day SMA of 203.36.\n\n**Investment Thesis**: The investment thesis is anchored in the robust fundamental performance of NVIDIA Corporation, which delivered $96.22 billion in revenue and $59.69 billion in net income for the July 2026 quarter. While the technical momentum, highlighted by a negative MACD histogram (-2.16) and a downward price trend, warrants caution, the consensus of the debate suggests the pullback to the 200-day SMA (203.36) and the Bollinger Lower Band (208.06) presents a high-quality opportunity for long-term investors. By adopting a moderate, scaled entry of 2.5% rather than a full 5% allocation, the strategy mitigates the 'cluster-risk' cited by the conservative analyst while avoiding the paralysis that would result from waiting for perfect MACD reversal signals. The bullish case will be invalidated if the stock decisively breaks and holds below the 200-day SMA, indicating a fundamental shift in market sentiment beyond mere cyclical correction.\n\n**Price Target**: not provided\n\n**Time Horizon**: 6-12 months",
